{
  "files": [
    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10\n#define DT 0.01f\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    int nbodies;\n    if (fread(&nbodies, sizeof(nbodies), 1, stdin) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    size_t count = (size_t)nbodies * 6;\n    float *tmp = (float *)malloc(count * sizeof(float));\n    if (!tmp) { perror(\"malloc\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n    if (fread(tmp, count * sizeof(float), 1, stdin) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    float * restrict px = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict py = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict pz = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vx = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vy = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vz = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    if (!px || !py || !pz || !vx || !vy || !vz) { perror(\"malloc\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        px[i] = tmp[6*i];\n        py[i] = tmp[6*i+1];\n        pz[i] = tmp[6*i+2];\n        vx[i] = tmp[6*i+3];\n        vy[i] = tmp[6*i+4];\n        vz[i] = tmp[6*i+5];\n    }\n    free(tmp);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n            #pragma omp for simd\n            for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n                float fx = 0.0f, fy = 0.0f, fz = 0.0f;\n                const float xi = px[i], yi = py[i], zi = pz[i];\n                for (int j = 0; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n                    float dx = px[j] - xi;\n                    float dy = py[j] - yi;\n                    float dz = pz[j] - zi;\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n                    fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n                    fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n                    fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n                }\n                vx[i] += DT*fx;\n                vy[i] += DT*fy;\n                vz[i] += DT*fz;\n            }\n\n            #pragma omp for simd\n            for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n                px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n                py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n                pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    float *out = (float *)malloc(count * sizeof(float));\n    if (!out) { perror(\"malloc\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        out[6*i]   = px[i];\n        out[6*i+1] = py[i];\n        out[6*i+2] = pz[i];\n        out[6*i+3] = vx[i];\n        out[6*i+4] = vy[i];\n        out[6*i+5] = vz[i];\n    }\n    if (fwrite(out, count * sizeof(float), 1, stdout) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    free(px); free(py); free(pz); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz); free(out);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using a Struct-of-Arrays layout with a single persistent OpenMP parallel region and combined `#pragma omp for simd` constructs allows each thread to process multiple bodies in SIMD lanes while preserving the exact per-body floating-point reduction order, reducing both thread-team creation overhead and improving memory locality.",
  "notes": "The inner j-loop remains scalar and sequential for every body i, so the accumulation order (and thus bit-exact output) is unchanged. The SoA layout enables contiguous vector loads of positions/velocities across bodies, and restrict qualifiers help the compiler prove no aliasing among arrays. A single parallel region spans all 10 iterations to avoid repeated thread-team creation.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Converted Body array-of-structs into separate Struct-of-Arrays (px/py/pz/vx/vy/vz)",
    "Hoisted the OpenMP parallel region outside the time-step loop",
    "Used combined worksharing-SIMD pragmas on both force and position-update loops",
    "Added restrict qualifiers to all array pointers to enable vectorization"
  ]
